.SH DESCRIPTION

The
.B auto-firewall-setup
command installs a simple firewall rule set and enables the
ipfw(8) firewall.

Caution: This script should not be run remotely via ssh, as
it may terminate and disable the network connection.
To enable a firewall
remotely, use a LOM (lights out management) remote console if
available.

.SH RETURN VALUES

0 on success, non-zero error codes otherwise.

